# 5. Question 2 — JOIN `order_items` and `products`

### Requirement

List every order item with the product name, category, price, and quantity ordered.

### Query

```sql
SELECT
    oi.order_item_id,
    oi.order_id,
    p.product_name,
    p.category,
    p.price,
    oi.quantity
FROM order_items oi
INNER JOIN products p
    ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
ORDER BY oi.order_id, oi.order_item_id;
```

### Explanation

This query joins `order_items` with `products` using `product_id`.

It allows management to see which products were included in orders, their categories and prices, and the quantities purchased.

### Result

**27 rows selected.**

This matches the 27 order items stored in the database.

