# 6. Question 3 — LEFT JOIN

### Requirement

List all customers and, where they exist, their orders, including customers who have never placed an order.

### Query

```sql
SELECT
    c.customer_id,
    c.customer_name,
    c.city,
    o.order_id,
    o.order_date
FROM customers c
LEFT JOIN orders o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
ORDER BY c.customer_id, o.order_date;
```

### Explanation

A `LEFT JOIN` is used because the query must keep **all customers**, even if a customer has no matching order.

If a customer has no order, the order-related columns will contain `NULL`.

### Result

The query returned the customer/order information while preserving the customer records required by the assignment.

