# 7. Question 4 — CTE and Customers Above Average Spending

### Requirement

Calculate each customer's total amount spent using:

`quantity × price`

Then return only customers whose spending is above the average customer spend.

### Query

```sql
WITH customer_totals AS (
    SELECT
        c.customer_id,
        c.customer_name,
        SUM(oi.quantity * p.price) AS total_spent
    FROM customers c
    JOIN orders o
        ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
    JOIN order_items oi
        ON o.order_id = oi.order_id
    JOIN products p
        ON oi.product_id = p.product_id
    GROUP BY c.customer_id, c.customer_name
),
average_spend AS (
    SELECT AVG(total_spent) AS avg_customer_spend
    FROM customer_totals
)
SELECT
    ct.customer_id,
    ct.customer_name,
    ct.total_spent
FROM customer_totals ct
CROSS JOIN average_spend a
WHERE ct.total_spent > a.avg_customer_spend
ORDER BY ct.total_spent DESC;
```

### Explanation

The first CTE, `customer_totals`, calculates the total spending for every customer.

The second CTE, `average_spend`, calculates the average of those customer totals.

The main query then returns only customers whose spending is greater than the average.

